---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on AdmitCost: none set, and how to verify it yourself" description="AdmitCost sets no cookie and keeps nothing in your browser storage: your score and family income stay in the page. How to check it in the developer tools of your browser." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>This site sets no cookie and uses no local storage. The SAT or ACT score and the family income you enter live only in the open page, and in its address if you copy the share link.</p>
    <h2>Why there is no consent banner</h2>
    <p>A consent banner is needed when a site stores or reads non-essential information on your device. Nothing of that kind happens here. {CLARITY_ID ? 'The stability monitoring described in the privacy policy runs without cookies and stores nothing on your device.' : 'No analytics or advertising script is loaded.'}</p>
    <h2>Verify it</h2>
    <p>Open the developer tools of your browser (F12 on most computers), then the Application or Storage tab, and look at Cookies and Local Storage while you change a university or an income: both stay empty, and the Network tab shows no request when the result changes.</p>
    <p>More in the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
